@database AmiDrop.guide
@node Main "AmiDrop 1.2"
@{b}AmiDrop 1.2@{ub}

Send files from a phone, tablet or computer directly to your Amiga.
No companion app is required.

AmiDrop requires AmigaOS 3.0+ and comes in two interchangeable versions.
They receive files in exactly the same way; only the interface differs:

  AmiDrop            GadTools, for classic screen modes. Needs nothing
                     beyond AmigaOS 3.0.
  AmiDrop_MUI        MUI edition by Jan Zahurancik / AmiKit.
                     Needs MUI 3.8 (muimaster.library 19) or newer.

@{b}Quick start@{ub}
1. Start AmiDrop.
2. Phone: scan the QR code.
3. PC: open the displayed address and enter the 6-digit code.
   If "No Code needed" is enabled, opening the address is enough.
4. Choose files and send them.

AmiDrop_MUI has a Copy to Clipboard button beside the address. With code
protection enabled it copies the session-protected link; with "No Code needed"
it copies the plain AmiDrop address. Paste it into a browser and nothing needs
typing on the other machine.

@{"Preferences" link Preferences}
