@node Preferences "Preferences"
@{b}Project > Preferences...@{ub}

Receive folder
  Where completed files are stored.

Max. file size
  512 KB, 1 MB, 5 MB, 10 MB, 25 MB, 50 MB, 100 MB, 250 MB, 500 MB or 1 GB.

TCP port
  Default: 8080. Valid range: 1024-65535.

Start server on launch
  If disabled, use Project > Start server.

No Code needed
  Disables the 6-digit access-code requirement. A browser that opens the
  displayed AmiDrop address can send files immediately. Use this only on a
  trusted local network. The main window shows "Deactivated by user" instead
  of a code while this option is active.

Ignore free-space check
  Normally AmiDrop requires the receive volume to hold the selected maximum
  file size plus a small safety reserve. Enable this only for intentionally
  small targets such as RAM: where you want to accept the risk of running out
  of space.

Show transfer information
  Shows the successful-transfer list and Clear list button in the lower part
  of the main window. If disabled, that section is hidden and the main window
  opens at a lower height.

Use
  Apply settings until AmiDrop is closed.

Save
  Apply and save settings permanently.

@{"Back" link Main}
@endnode

@node Safety "Safety and failed transfers"
AmiDrop writes incoming data to ADROP.PART first.
Only a complete transfer is renamed to the final filename.

If a transfer is aborted, times out, loses the network connection or cannot be
written to disk, the partial file is removed.

With code protection enabled, five wrong login attempts lock access for
30 seconds. QR tokens and access codes are recreated whenever the server is
restarted. If "No Code needed" is enabled, anyone who can reach the AmiDrop
address on the local network can send files.

@{"Back" link Main}
@endnode

@node ToolTypes "ToolTypes"
Workbench ToolTypes and CLI assignments:

PORT=8080
MAXSIZEKB=51200
RECEIVEDIR=Work:Downloads/AmiDrop
STARTSERVER=YES
NOCODENEEDED=NO
IGNORESPACE=NO
SHOWTRANSFERINFO=YES

STARTSERVER, NOCODENEEDED, IGNORESPACE and SHOWTRANSFERINFO accept YES/NO, TRUE/FALSE, ON/OFF or 1/0.
MAXSIZEKB is the precise limit in KB. Legacy MAXSIZE values in whole MB are
still accepted.

For WBStartup, the standard Workbench DONOTWAIT ToolType may also be used.
AmiDrop ignores reserved Workbench ToolTypes.

@{"Back" link Main}
@endnode

@node Troubleshooting "Troubleshooting"
No IP address shown
  Check that the TCP/IP stack is online and the Amiga has an IPv4 address.

Port already in use
  Choose another port in Preferences.

Cannot write file
  Check that the receive volume is mounted, writable and has enough space.

Phone cannot connect
  The phone and Amiga must be able to reach each other on the network.
  Scan the current QR code again after a server restart.

  Very old TCP/IP stacks such as MIAMI may cause problems with incoming TCP
  connections even when the Amiga can still be pinged from another device.
  If this occurs, switch to a current TCP/IP stack such as Roadshow.

@{"Back" link Main}
@endnode

